# Documented CVE suppressions. This file applies to ALL THREE image scans (trivy-api,
# trivy-web, trivy-mcp), so an entry hides that CVE everywhere — including in an image
# that later gains the package for an unrelated reason. Every entry needs: the package,
# why it is unreachable, and the condition for removing it. Remove entries as soon as
# that condition holds (ROADMAP UP-1 removed CVE-2026-33671, picomatch via sqlite3's
# node-gyp, once sqlite3 became a devDependency and picomatch left every image).
